            <ArticleTitle>A remnant sewing needle in the right ventricle as a cause of chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E23-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/clc.20530</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sewing needles, albeit a rare case of penetrating cardiac injury, are potentially life-threatening. We report a case of a self-inflicted remnant intracardiac sewing needle which is diagnosed with nonspecific chest pain and successfully extracted 23 months after its insertion.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright 2010 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
